    "methods_description": "Patients were monitored simultaneously with standard video-EEG (10-20 system or 25-electrode array) and the Sensor Dot (SD) wearable device, which recorded behind-the-ear EEG at 250 Hz along with ECG, EMG, and movement data (accelerometer/gyroscope at 25 Hz) via a second module on the chest. Electrode placement for the wearable EEG was tailored to each patient's suspected seizure onset hemisphere, yielding same-side and cross-head channels or additional lateral channels for generalized presentations.",
